      {
        "text": "He supports cutting federal taxes for middle-class families and expanding the child tax credit. He opposes measures that would raise energy costs. He proposes fighting regulations and unfunded mandates that drive up local taxes and housing costs. He favors reducing healthcare expenses through price transparency and market competition. He supports expanded telehealth and preventive care. On immigration, he calls for securing the border and reforming asylum rules. His campaign says he backs an America First economic agenda, including tariffs to protect American workers and making the Trump tax cuts permanent. He has expressed concern about the expansion of executive power. He says Congress should reclaim its constitutional role on tariffs and spending. He signed a pledge to support a term limits amendment limiting House members to three terms and senators to two. The Elburn Village Board passed a resolution opposing the BUILD Act. He said the legislation would reduce local zoning authority. He says his experience as mayor includes managing government budgets and making difficult decisions about priorities.",
